{"kind":"table","sheet":"FluxSpecification","address":"A1:F23","rows":23,"cols":6,"values":[[null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"Instructor flux specification",null,null,null,null],[null,"Completed paired amount-flux equations for notebook 03.",null,null,null,null],[null,"Teaching worksheet only. Editing this file does not change model_definition.xlsx or the simulation.",null,null,null,null],[null,"Source: course workbook + teaching_specification.py; https://gmd.copernicus.org/articles/18/1155/2025/#section3",null,null,null,null],[null,"Process ID","Process / arrow","J_DIC (mol C/yr)","J_TA (eq/yr)","Inputs / hint"],[null,"Q_*","Water: i -> j","rho_i Q_ij DIC_i(t)","rho_i Q_ij TA_i(t)","Q_ij: water volume transport (m3/yr), from thc / mixing. Use source density and concentration."],[null,"G_L / G_H","Gas: atm -> surface i (signed)","v_i A_i [K0_i pCO2_atm(t) - c_i(t)]","0","piston_velocity, area; K0_i and c_i from local chemistry. Invasion minus outgassing."],[null,"POC","Organic export: L_b -> D_b","P_0","0","P_0 = poc_export; fixed, fully remineralized at depth; DIC-only closure."],[null,"PIC","Carbonate export: L_b -> module","E(t) = r P_0","2 E(t)","r = rain_ratio (PIC/POC); CaCO3 formation removes 1 carbon and 2 TA equivalents."],[null,"W","Weathering: outside -> L_b","W_0","2 W_0","W_0 = weathering_dic; the model adds 2 TA equivalents per mole of DIC."],[null,"D","Dissolution: module -> D_b","D(t) [supplied response]","2 D(t)","D = sediment_response(E, DIC_d, TA_d, z_snow; T_d, S_d, p_d, alpha, z0). Reverse CaCO3 formation."],[null,"B_net","Net burial: module -> outside (signed)","B_net(t) = E(t) - D(t)","2 B_net(t)","Compare carbonate rain and dissolution, including old sediment; residual, not an extra drain."],[null,null,null,null,null,null],[null,"Conventions and supplied hints (symbolic equations, not Excel calculation formulas)",null,null,null,null],[null,"Positive follows the arrow: subtract at source, add at destination. DIC tracks carbon even when carried as CO2 or particles.",null,null,null,null],[null,"DIC_i(t), TA_i(t): mol C/kg, eq/kg. P_0 = poc_export; r = rain_ratio; W_0 = weathering_dic. d means D_b.",null,null,null,null],[null,"Gas: c_i(t) = chemistry(DIC_i(t), TA_i(t); T_i, S_i, p_i); c_eq,i(t) = K0_i pCO2_atm(t). Both concentrations: mol/m3.",null,null,null,null],[null,"v_i: m/yr; A_i: m2. K0_i is local solubility in compatible pressure units; p_i is water pressure, distinct from atmospheric pCO2.",null,null,null,null],[null,"D(t) uses the supplied sediment response above. z_snow is sediment memory; alpha and z0 are workbook parameters. No extra sediment C stock.",null,null,null,null],[null,"Fixed water mass m_i = rho_i V_i [kg]. Internal dissolved transfer: dX_i/dt = -J_X/m_i; dX_j/dt = +J_X/m_j (X = DIC or TA).",null,null,null,null],[null,"Q_ij is water volume transport [m3/yr]; rho_i Q_ij converts to kg/yr. The benchmark retains its nominal litre conversion (03.3).",null,null,null,null],[null,"Weathering assumes 1 mol DIC : 2 TA equivalents. Real riverine input need not have exactly this ratio.",null,null,null,null]]}
